# Emotes and spells for Romeo and Juliet; see plays/muchado.actions for the format.
# Paris's, Romeo's and Juliet's deaths and Juliet's last kiss are picked up
# automatically from the stage directions.

# The ball (Act 1, Scene 5): two kisses, the second has no stage direction.
ROMEO    | Kissing her                   | /kiss @Juliet
ROMEO    | Give me my sin again          | /kiss @Juliet

# Stage fights: "duel @Role" challenges that role's player to a real duel
# (where duels are allowed); "yield" forfeits it when the script says so.

# The opening brawl (Act 1, Scene 1); the Prince parts them, so Benvolio
# yields once it's over.
TYBALT   | Have at thee, coward          | duel @Benvolio
BENVOLIO | Here were the servants        | yield

# Mercutio is wounded, then Tybalt is killed (Act 3, Scene 1).
MERCUTIO | Come, sir, your passado        | duel @Tybalt
MERCUTIO | I am hurt                     | yield
ROMEO    | This shall determine that     | duel @Tybalt
TYBALT   | They fight; Tybalt falls      | yield Feign Death /lie

# Juliet takes the Friar's potion (Act 4, Scene 3) and seems dead.
JULIET   | Romeo, Romeo, Romeo, here’s drink | use Refreshing Spring Water
JULIET   | Throws herself on the bed     | Feign Death /sleep

# The tomb (Act 5, Scene 3). Romeo kills Paris, then drinks the poison;
# water, not wine.
ROMEO    | Wilt thou provoke me          | duel @Paris
PARIS    | O, I am slain                 | yield
ROMEO    | O true apothecary             | use Refreshing Spring Water
JULIET   | Kisses him                    | /kiss @Romeo
